# CloudWatch Monitoring

## Overview

Add CloudWatch Alarms for Lambda errors, throttles, duration, SQS queue depth, and DynamoDB throttles. Notify via SNS for critical failures. Use CDK to define alarms and optional dashboards.

## Lambda Alarms

```typescript
// cdk/lib/stacks/monitoring-stack.ts

import { Stack, StackProps, Duration } from "aws-cdk-lib";
import { Construct } from "constructs";
import {
  Alarm,
  ComparisonOperator,
  TreatMissingData,
  Stats,
} from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch";
import { SnsAction } from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch-actions";
import { Topic } from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-sns";
import { Function as LambdaFunction } from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-lambda";

interface MonitoringStackProps extends StackProps {
  lambdaFunctions: LambdaFunction[];
  alarmTopic?: Topic;
}

export class MonitoringStack extends Stack {
  constructor(scope: Construct, id: string, props: MonitoringStackProps) {
    super(scope, id, props);

    const alarmTopic =
      props.alarmTopic ??
      new Topic(this, "AlarmTopic", { displayName: "Real Estate Alarms" });

    for (const fn of props.lambdaFunctions) {
      new Alarm(this, `${fn.node.id}Errors`, {
        alarmName: `${fn.functionName}-errors`,
        metric: fn.metricErrors({ period: Duration.minutes(1) }),
        threshold: 5,
        evaluationPeriods: 1,
        comparisonOperator: ComparisonOperator.GREATER_THAN_THRESHOLD,
        treatMissingData: TreatMissingData.NOT_BREACHING,
      }).addAlarmAction(new SnsAction(alarmTopic));

      new Alarm(this, `${fn.node.id}Throttles`, {
        alarmName: `${fn.functionName}-throttles`,
        metric: fn.metricThrottles({ period: Duration.minutes(1) }),
        threshold: 1,
        evaluationPeriods: 1,
        comparisonOperator: ComparisonOperator.GREATER_THAN_THRESHOLD,
        treatMissingData: TreatMissingData.NOT_BREACHING,
      }).addAlarmAction(new SnsAction(alarmTopic));

      const timeoutMs = fn.timeout?.toMilliseconds() ?? 30000;
      new Alarm(this, `${fn.node.id}Duration`, {
        alarmName: `${fn.functionName}-duration`,
        metric: fn.metricDuration({ period: Duration.minutes(1), statistic: Stats.P99 }),
        threshold: timeoutMs * 0.8,
        evaluationPeriods: 2,
        comparisonOperator: ComparisonOperator.GREATER_THAN_THRESHOLD,
        treatMissingData: TreatMissingData.NOT_BREACHING,
      }).addAlarmAction(new SnsAction(alarmTopic));
    }
  }
}
```

## SQS Queue Depth

```typescript
import { Metric } from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch";
import { Queue } from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-sqs";

for (const queue of props.queues ?? []) {
  new Alarm(this, `QueueDepth-${queue.node.id}`, {
    alarmName: `sqs-${queue.queueName}-depth`,
    metric: new Metric({
      namespace: "AWS/SQS",
      metricName: "ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible",
      dimensionsMap: { QueueName: queue.queueName },
      period: Duration.minutes(5),
      statistic: Stats.SUM,
    }),
    threshold: 1000,
    evaluationPeriods: 2,
    comparisonOperator: ComparisonOperator.GREATER_THAN_THRESHOLD,
    treatMissingData: TreatMissingData.NOT_BREACHING,
  }).addAlarmAction(new SnsAction(alarmTopic));
}
```

## DynamoDB Consumed Capacity

For provisioned tables, alarm on throttled requests. For PAY_PER_REQUEST, optional alarms on user errors or system errors.

## Dashboard (Optional)

```typescript
import { Dashboard, GraphWidget } from "aws-cdk-lib/aws-cloudwatch";

const dashboard = new Dashboard(this, "Dashboard", {
  dashboardName: "RealEstate",
  defaultInterval: Duration.hours(3),
});

props.lambdaFunctions.forEach((fn) => {
  dashboard.addWidgets(
    new GraphWidget({
      title: `${fn.functionName} invocations`,
      left: [fn.metricInvocations()],
      width: 12,
    }),
    new GraphWidget({
      title: `${fn.functionName} errors`,
      left: [fn.metricErrors()],
      width: 12,
    })
  );
});
```

## Conventions

- Alarm on Lambda errors, throttles, and P99 duration (e.g. > 80% of timeout)
- Use SNS topic for alarm actions; subscribe email or Slack in separate step
- Set `treatMissingData: NOT_BREACHING` to avoid alarms when there is no traffic
- Tune thresholds and evaluation periods per environment (stricter in prod)
- Use dashboards for operational visibility; alarms for alerting

## Anti-Patterns

- No alarms for critical Lambdas or queues
- Alarm on every single error (use threshold and evaluation periods)
- Missing SNS subscription for alarm actions
- TreatMissingData BREACHING when no data means no traffic

